~ start
???: You have arrived. I was waiting for you. [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/archivist_normal.png]
???: We met when you first crossed into this world.
Archivist: I am the Magical Archivist of this castle.
Archivist: I am responsible for all the magical writings and prophecies that speak about both the past and the future of the Lands of the Prism. 
Archivist: I do not need sight to read a prophecy. But the magic must speak clearly. And I have a problem with the prophecy I have been analyzing today. [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/archivist_sad.png]
Archivist: My magical screen reader cannot make sense of the description attached to this orb. It just says: "Visual prophecy underscore final dot magic". What is it supposed to mean? [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/crystall_ball.png]
Archivist: I fear this may be important... 
: You activate your power to perceive the world as she does. [#activate_shader] [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/crystall_ball_prophecy.png]
: The world fades to darkness. Through the Mirror of Resonance, you experience the world as the Archivist does.
: The problem is not the orb itself, but the text used to describe it.
: You should try to help her! Read more about this problem in the Resonance Codex. [#show_debug] [#minigame_menu] 

=> END

~ fail_reaction
Archivist: No... the screen reader is still reading something unclear. I cannot understand the prophecy.
=> END

~ win_reaction
Archivist: "A dragon flying over a burning castle"... Now the prophecy speaks clearly. [#deactivate_shader] 
Archivist: It is Kalipso!!! The great dragon is returning! You must hurry! [#close_minigame] [#portrait=res://scenes/cutscenes/images/prophecy_expanded.png]
Archivist: You have to reach the Herald immediately. She can make a royal announcement and warn the whole realm! We need a hero to save us from the dragon!
Archivist: She usually wanders around the castle. Go look for her!
=> END

~ already_helped
Archivist: Hurry! You have to find the Herald! She should be somewhere in the castle!
=> END